Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-15-2000||02:15 PM||||How well does this work? I am running rich and want to get rid of some possibilities. What brand should I buy? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||08-15-2000||04:18 PM||||If you're running rich I doubt an injector cleaner will do much of anything.  Try changing the O2 sensor......it is usually the root of lean or rich conditions (unless there is something more seriously wrong).<P>As far as what brand to use, I would use BG products.  Ed Parks sells a "de-carb" kit that is made by BG.  It dissolves all of the carbon deposits in the intake system, including the fuel injectors.  <P>Cost is $40 + shipping (last I heard) and is well worth the $$.  Contact Ed at<P>fierofactory@juno.com       <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike Valentine<BR>Brighton, Colorado<BR>Mile High Fieros<BR>'88 GT 16K mi.<BR>'88 GT 121K mi.||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||08-15-2000||04:42 PM||||The ECM said it was running rich. Switched the O2 sensor, and then it said Lean, but now it's back to rich?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||08-15-2000||05:11 PM||||Try clearing the codes (unplug battery for about 30 sec-1 min.).  Sometimes the computer will continue to trip codes even after that item has been fixed/replaced.<P>If that doesn't do it, then we'll need to troubleshoot some more.  ||||reg||1
